body:
### Tested versions

- Reproducible in v4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e], v3.5.2.stable, master branch

### System information

Godot v4.6.1.stable - Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm) 12 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon Graphics (renoir, LLVM 15.0.6, DRM 3.49, 6.1.0-42-amd64) - AMD Ryzen 5 PRO 4650U with Radeon Graphics (12 threads) - 14.85 GiB memory

### Issue description

Web audio input samples are not guaranteed to be within -1.0 and 1.0, such as when all browser preprocessing is disabled (automatic gain control, echo cancellation, noise suppression). There is no clamping before converting to int16, so it just overflows. This ends up causing a lot of crackling when the mic input is really loud, which is far worse than just hard limiting it (which is what I would normally expect it to do).

### Steps to reproduce

I personally just use Audacity to generate a sine wave with an amplitude of 1.0, and then I use Helvum to route Audacity's output into Firefox. (you can also just do something loud with your mic, like blowing on it)

In order to disable browser mic preprocessing, I came up with a somewhat hacky solution since there doesn't seem to be an official way to do it, so I made this small script that is supposed to be run before Godot loads:

```javascript
const originalGetUserMedia = navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia.bind(navigator.mediaDevices);

navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia = function(constraints) {
    if (!constraints.audio) {
        constraints.audio = {};
    }

    if (constraints.audio === true) {
        constraints.audio = {};
    }

    constraints.audio.echoCancellation = false;
    constraints.audio.noiseSuppression = false;
    constraints.audio.autoGainControl = false;

    return originalGetUserMedia(constraints);
};
```
You can either add it in export settings via HTML > Head Include (this won't work if you use One-click deploy i think), or use a userscript manager like Tampermonkey (what I did).

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

The repro is just an AudioStreamMicrophone that autoplays, so it's not enough to trigger the issue without the conditions described above.
[overflow-repro.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26727688/overflow-repro.zip)
